================================================================================
Z_7-invariant cores: 2/16 -- the descended cores are GENERALLY NOT Z_7^*-invariant
(their residues mod 7 are not multiplier-orbit unions). So the PURE Z_7 cyclotomic SOS does
NOT directly apply -- the transitive symmetry must be MANUFACTURED by Z_7^*-AVERAGING = the
Gamma_0(14) congruence (HYP-3553). Demonstrate the averaging symmetrizes the apex Gram:

   example NON-invariant core residues [1, 3, 5] (= O_1 of consec):
     raw apex Gram spectrum:        [9.0, 0.308, 0.643, 5.049, 5.049, 0.643, 0.308] (NOT flat => SET-DEPENDENT)
     Z_7^*-averaged (Gamma_0) spec: [9.0, 0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 0.25] (FLAT off-0 => SET-INDEP)
   => the raw Gram of a non-invariant core is non-flat/set-dependent; averaging over the
   multiplier (the Gamma_0(14) congruence) FLATTENS it to the cyclotomic form, SET-INDEPENDENT
   -- 'manufacture the transitive symmetry it lacks'. (Caveat: complement-of-a-point cores
   like {0..5} are already flat -- it is set-INVARIANCE, not flatness per se, that fails.)

================================================================================
CONCLUSION: the descended cores are NOT pure-Z_7-invariant (covering kills the apex-7 grid,
residues not multiplier-closed). So rho_j>=c is NOT closed by a bare cyclotomic SOS; it needs
the Gamma_0(14) congruence AVERAGING over Z_7^* to MANUFACTURE the transitive symmetry, after
which the averaged Gram is flat/cyclotomic and SET-INDEPENDENT (= klein-S8's inf R'=0.344 >=
1/(2 zeta(2))). The mechanism is congruence-averaging (Gamma_0(14)), not bare Z_7 -- this
SHARPENS the proof path: the next step is the Han-Lee Gamma_0(14) 2nd-moment constant.
================================================================================
